lete the day after inspectors sign the paperwork. We do not need an 18-month regulatory review before deployment. We need automated circuit breakers that escalate decisions to human supervisors the instant a system approaches operational limits.\n\nReal-time telemetry and immutable flight recorders isolate system failures in milliseconds, making compensation direct and remediation rapid. Look at your local power bill and watch how regional grid operators handle industrial data centers. Do not let monopolies hide behind utility rules while socializing their capital expenses. Demand open competition, hard stop-switches at operational boundaries, and direct corporate liability for every kilowatt and line of code they run.",
